WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.834
-Our first guest stars
as Santa Claus

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:05.767
in the new animated comedy
series "Santa Inc.,"

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:09.067
which begins streaming tomorrow
on HBO Max.

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:11.934
Here's the one and only Seth
Rogen, ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:14.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
Ah! Ah!

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.734
It's great to see you. Ah!

00:00:16.734 --> 00:00:19.801
It's great to see you.
-Good to be here.

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:22.000
-I almost like you
being on a giant screen.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.601
-This is much better.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:25.601
If I was there, I would ask
if I could touch

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:27.133
Machine Gun Kelly's pants,
though.

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:28.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.868
-You would want to touch it.

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:33.367
-They look cool.
-Yeah, he's a rock star.

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:36.200
-You can't change your name back
from Machine Gun.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.767
Your name's Machine Gun.
-No.

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:40.434
-Leave it Machine Gun!
-No, no. He goes back.

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:42.367
He goes back and forth, man.

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:44.834
Did you ever have a nickname
or try to have a nickname?

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:47.667
-No. And if I had one
as cool as Machine Gun,

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:49.267
I would stick with it.
If you ever knew me

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:50.601
as Machine Gun Rogen,

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:52.033
that's all you would
ever know me as.

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:53.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:58.534
-I want to say happy holidays
to you and your lovely wife.

00:00:58.534 --> 00:01:01.734
I know in Canada you celebrate
Thanksgiving earlier

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:03.000
than we celebrate Thanksgiving.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.133
Is that October? Am I way late?

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:09.067
-They do. I didn't celebrate it
growing up, honestly.

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:13.234
And it's because my parents
always told me that

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:17.200
Jewish people did not celebrate
Thanksgiving in Canada.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.100
Something that I later found
to be not true at all.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.133
It was a lie they told us
because they didn't want to go

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:28.467
through, like, the hassle of
doing Thanksgiving.

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:31.934
And so they fabricated
that Jews didn't do that.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:33.801
-Oh, my God.
-I don't know why, in my head.

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:35.133
-Of course,
you got to believe them

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:36.467
and just go, "Yeah, yeah.
Of course not."

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:38.801
But wow. What a lie.
-It seemed legit.

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:41.501
Jews deprive themselves
of a lot of great things.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.367
[ Laughter ]
We don't eat bacon.

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:45.501
It added up.

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:48.367
If we're not eating bacon,
all bets are off.

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:50.367
Who knows what we're not doing?

00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:52.467
So yeah. But now they do it.

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:54.067
It's funny. Now that I have
nephews, they do it.

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:56.200
-I have to ask you about this,
'cause a few weeks ago,

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.601
I was watching -- everyone
watching, the big Adele concert

00:01:59.601 --> 00:02:02.701
that was this big concert
special, the big spectacle.

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:04.300
And who do I see
in the audience?

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.067
Seth Rogen.

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.367
-Yeah, I was there.

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:10.734
I was in the front row
of the Adele concert.

00:02:10.734 --> 00:02:15.200
And that is as surprising to me
as anyone

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:20.334
because I had no idea
I was attending the taping

00:02:20.334 --> 00:02:24.367
of an Adele television special
at all.

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:25.934
I got an invitation --

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:28.334
"Do you want to go to
a small Adele concert,"

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:31.033
is what I remember absorbing.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:33.000
And I go to my wife Laurie,

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.467
"You want to go to this small
Adele concert?"

00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:35.734
"Great, sounds fun."

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:38.734
It's at Griffith Park.
That sounds cool.

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:43.000
So, if I'm being honest --
I hate to burst everyone's --

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.634
I smoke weed, Jimmy.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.634 --> 00:02:46.901
And me and my wife --
-Breaking news.

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:49.467
Breaking news here.
-I know. It's tough.

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:51.868
But you'll have to
reconcile that.

00:02:51.868 --> 00:02:53.734
So we were like,
"It's an Adele concert.

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:55.968
It's in the park."
We smoked a ton of weed.

00:02:55.968 --> 00:02:57.701
And we're like,
"We're just gonna go

00:02:57.701 --> 00:03:00.234
and enjoy this lovely Adele
concert."

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:05.133
We pull up and we see cranes --
camera cranes.

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:06.834
There's drones flying around.

00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:09.367
There's an entire crew there.

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:12.300
And I'm like, "Oh, no, we are
at the filming

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.167
of a television special,
I think.

00:03:15.167 --> 00:03:16.667
We're on a television show."

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:18.934
And I'm like, "Maybe it's not
that big a television special."

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:21.033
And then the first person I see
is Oprah Winfrey.

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.601
And I'm like, "Oh, no. I think
it's a big television special."

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:25.000
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.534
-And then me and my wife
were like, "Okay.

00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:29.100
Maybe we can just kind of like
slink into the background."

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.133
You know?
Like we'll just sit in the back.

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:33.234
It's fine.

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:35.767
We are not equipped mentally
to deal with

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:37.601
doing this right now, really.

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:40.801
And so we go up to the desk
and they give us our tickets,

00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:44.467
and our seat numbers literally
are 1A and 1B.

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:45.501
[ Laughter ]
And I'm like, "Oh, no!"

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:46.701
-It doesn't get bigger!

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:47.934
-That sounds close!

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:50.701
-Yeah, it sounds real close.

00:03:50.701 --> 00:03:55.334
-So we go to 1A and 1B,
and we're in the front row.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:56.601
We're in front-row center.

00:03:56.601 --> 00:03:59.667
We're as close as you can
fathomably be. I sit down.

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:02.667
There's like a camera literally
just pointed at my face.

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:04.868
-Do you know Adele?

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:08.400
-I have never met --
No! I don't know Adele!

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.767
And if, Adele, you're watching
this, why did you do that?

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:14.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:15.868
Because the whole time I'm like,

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:19.100
"There are so many more famous
people than me here

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.534
who should be sitting
where I'm sitting."

00:04:21.534 --> 00:04:24.767
And I could just, like, feel
them be insulted

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:26.467
that I had such a good seat.

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:28.534
Like, I was in front of Drake.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:32.000
Like, there's no world where
I should be in front of Drake.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.100
How is that possible?

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.767
And I could just feel, like,
Drake's eyes, like, drilling

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:41.200
into the back of my head like,
"Why am I in 3R and he's in 1A?"

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:44.934
I was six rows in front of
Ellen DeGeneres and Kris Jenner.

00:04:44.934 --> 00:04:50.133
Like, I truly have no idea
why they did that.

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:51.968
It was truly wild.

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:55.601
-What do you do when the camera
turns on you?

00:04:55.601 --> 00:04:56.934
What do you do at
an Adele concert?

00:04:56.934 --> 00:05:00.100
Did you clap or sing along or --

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:01.400
-You try to look --
I don't know.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.367
The whole time, I'm like,
"Just try to look cool,"

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:05.467
which is not a healthy thought
to have.

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:07.567
And for me at an Adele --

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:11.434
It was hard for me to look cool
'cause I'm uncomfortable.

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:14.934
I'm too close.
I feel, like, Leonardo DiCaprio

00:05:14.934 --> 00:05:17.133
behind me thinking like,
"Did Seth Rogen write

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:19.167
'Rolling in the Deep'?
Is that why he's so close?"

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:21.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.601 --> 00:05:23.701
I feel out of place.

00:05:23.701 --> 00:05:28.701
And so I try to just --
It looked like I very actively

00:05:28.701 --> 00:05:32.400
tried to look like I'm enjoying
this Adele concert, which I was.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.701
But I was very distracted by
the fact that I was on camera.

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:38.634
So I was playing the role of
just an undistracted,

00:05:38.634 --> 00:05:42.000
normal, cool guy trying to enjoy
an Adele concert.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:45.200
-Well, weirdly enough, I put
together a quick little montage

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.000
of you enjoying
the Adele concert.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:48.267
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, no.

00:05:48.267 --> 00:05:51.033
-Let's take a look at
Seth Rogen.

00:05:51.033 --> 00:05:55.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:55.133 --> 00:06:01.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.234 --> 00:06:03.133
-It was live.

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:04.501
A lot of standing.
-Yeah.

00:06:04.501 --> 00:06:05.834
-Every time, I was just like,

00:06:05.834 --> 00:06:07.267
"Are we standing
after every song?"

00:06:07.267 --> 00:06:08.667
That was also one of
those things.

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:11.367
"We're standing every time?
Every song?"

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:13.300
-Dude, that's fantastic.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:15.334
-But everyone I know watched it.

00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:18.567
It was -- I think it's the most
popular thing I've ever been in

00:06:18.567 --> 00:06:20.601
in my entire life.

00:06:20.601 --> 00:06:22.601
There's people who I know
have not watched

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:24.767
my last five movies who have
been texting me, being like,

00:06:24.767 --> 00:06:26.901
"That Adele concert looked
incredible."

00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:28.767
[ Laughter ]
That's wild.

00:06:28.767 --> 00:06:31.367
-You got great reviews.
Good. I'm glad.

00:06:31.367 --> 00:06:33.000
-Very good, rave reviews.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:36.834
-I want to talk to you also,
but I heard -- it's not a rumor.

00:06:36.834 --> 00:06:39.033
I guess you actually are
the voice of Donkey Kong

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:41.100
in the new
"Super Mario Bros." movie.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:44.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I am.

00:06:44.834 --> 00:06:47.868
-I think that would be
a dream come true

00:06:47.868 --> 00:06:50.534
to anyone who plays video --
I loved "Donkey Kong."

00:06:50.534 --> 00:06:52.601
I mean, it's legendary.
-I love "Donkey Kong."

00:06:52.601 --> 00:06:55.033
Yeah, and I think --
Yeah, it was an --

00:06:55.033 --> 00:06:57.934
It was not an expected call
to get.

00:06:57.934 --> 00:07:00.100
As I was playing "Donkey Kong"
as a child,

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:03.167
I never projected myself onto
that character necessarily.

00:07:03.167 --> 00:07:04.901
But no, it's a thrill.

00:07:04.901 --> 00:07:06.267
My mom is very proud of me.

00:07:06.267 --> 00:07:07.801
Everyone's very proud of me.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:07.801 --> 00:07:10.968
-Your mom, by the way,
who I follow on Twitter --

00:07:10.968 --> 00:07:12.100
I don't know if that's weird

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.367
that I follow your mom
on Twitter, but --

00:07:13.367 --> 00:07:15.434
-Not at all.
-She makes me laugh.

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:17.300
Your parents have been
to the show many times.

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:18.801
And tell her I said hello.

00:07:18.801 --> 00:07:20.534
She sent out this tweet
that made me laugh.

00:07:20.534 --> 00:07:22.334
She said...

00:07:22.334 --> 00:07:23.934
"My son is Donkey Kong.

00:07:23.934 --> 00:07:25.868
Don't really know what to say
about that."

00:07:25.868 --> 00:07:31.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:31.167 --> 00:07:32.834
She's got great delivery, man.

00:07:32.834 --> 00:07:35.334
She writes good jokes.
[ Laughs ]

00:07:35.334 --> 00:07:36.934
She writes good jokes.

00:07:36.934 --> 00:07:39.167
-It is funny.
-It is funny.

00:07:39.167 --> 00:07:41.701
-That's the type of support
and encouragement I get at home

00:07:41.701 --> 00:07:43.968
for my career.
-They what made you who you are.

00:07:43.968 --> 00:07:45.868
Exactly, right? I love Mom.

00:07:45.868 --> 00:07:47.334
I want to talk to you about
your funny new

00:07:47.334 --> 00:07:49.434
animated series "Santa Inc."
when we come back.

00:07:49.434 --> 00:07:50.801
More with Seth Rogen,
ladies and gentlemen.

